## Test Anti-Pattern Audit: `ProductCatalogTests.cs`

### Summary

| Severity | Count |
|----------|-------|
| **Critical** | 5 |
| **High** | 1 |
| **Medium** | 2 |

This is a textbook **coverage-touching** test suite. Every public method is invoked, giving 95%+ line coverage, but almost nothing is actually verified. Bugs in pricing logic, search filtering, CSV formatting, and deletion would all slip through undetected.

---

### 🔴 Critical Findings

#### 1. Systematic Coverage-Touching (entire class)

The suite methodically calls every public member with no meaningful assertions. 5 of 10 tests have **zero assertions**; the remaining 5 use only `Assert.IsNotNull` which merely confirms a non-null reference was returned — never that the *correct value* was returned.

#### 2. No Assertions — `AddProduct_Works` (line 17)

```csharp
// BEFORE – proves nothing
_catalog.AddProduct(product);

// FIX
_catalog.AddProduct(product);
var retrieved = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", retrieved!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, retrieved.Price);
```

#### 3. No Assertions — `UpdatePrice_Works` (line 33)

The core pricing logic is never verified. A bug like `Price = newPrice + 1` passes silently.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.UpdatePrice("SKU-001", 14.99m);
var updated = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual(14.99m, updated!.Price);
```

#### 4. No Assertions — `RemoveProduct_Works` (line 39)

Deletion is never confirmed. A no-op `Delete` passes.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.RemoveProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.IsNull(_catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001"));
```

#### 5. No Assertions — `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (line 69)

The discount math (`Price * (1 - fraction)`) is the highest-risk logic and is completely unverified.

```csharp
// FIX
_catalog.ApplyBulkDiscount(0.10m);
Assert.AreEqual(8.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001")!.Price);
Assert.AreEqual(17.991m, _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-002")!.Price);
```

#### 6. No Assertions — `ImportFromCsv_Works` (line 85) & trivial assertion in `ExportToCsv_Works` (line 77)

Import/export are never round-tripped or content-checked.

```csharp
// FIX – ImportFromCsv
_catalog.ImportFromCsv("SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
var imported = _catalog.GetProduct("SKU-001");
Assert.AreEqual("Widget", imported!.Name);
Assert.AreEqual(9.99m, imported.Price);

// FIX – ExportToCsv
var csv = _catalog.ExportToCsv();
StringAssert.Contains(csv, "SKU-001,Widget,9.99");
```

---

